  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TRANSFORMING LANNPLUS TO NUTRITION SMART COMMUNITIES A RIGHTS-BASED APPROACH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will target a total population of 49,985 and 78,276 in Pujehun and Port Loko districts respectively, with the aim of tackling maternal and child malnutrition through systematic screening, development of nutrition-sensitive community plans in addition to the LANN+ approach (i.e. nutrition education; nutrition-sensitive agriculture; sustainable natural resources management; nutrition-sensitive WASH and Income and market linkages). Year two will also involve the addition of 30 new communities (15 each on the WHH and CWW operational zones) to expand on the benefits of the project to other beneficiaries in dire need of this kind of intervention.</narrative>
  </description>
